;; Diameter (RFC 6733) is a flat header + AVP TLV wire format, like its
;; predecessor RADIUS — not ASN.1, so there is no BER/DER layer to reuse
;; from org-ietf-asn1 (see README's "Why there is no dependency on
;; org-ietf-asn1"). No cryptographic primitive is needed either: unlike
;; RADIUS, which needs MD5 for its own Authenticator/User-Password
;; obfuscation (org-ietf-radius's `radius.md5`), Diameter delegates
;; transport security entirely to TLS/DTLS (RFC 6733 §5.3, §13) and this
;; repo is a codec, not a transport — nothing here computes an
;; Authenticator-equivalent value.
{:paths ["src"]
 :deps {
        io.github.kotoba-lang/test {:local/root "../kotoba.test"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/text {:local/root "../kotoba.text"}}
 :aliases
 {:test {:extra-paths ["test"]}
  :cljs {:extra-paths ["test"]}}}
